course: dictionary
lesson: 4157
title: Gnat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gnat is a tiny flying insect, a bit like a very small fly. You will often see gnats in a cloud near water, especially on summer evenings.
explain: Read this: «Bats catch moths and gnats in the dark by shouting very high squeaks and listening for the echoes.» Bats catch gnats, so gnats must be small creatures that are eaten. The words around gnat give you the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Bats catch moths and tiny flies in the dark» still makes sense, so gnat means something like a tiny fly. Some kinds of gnat bite, so take care on summer evenings.
fact: A gnat is a tiny flying insect, a bit like a very small fly.
fact: Gnats often gather in clouds near water, and some kinds bite.
fact: In science, gnats are insects with six legs and two wings.
fact: Many gnats are food for birds, bats and fish.
fact: «Strain at a gnat» means to fuss over tiny things.
exercise: «Watch bats round a streetlamp at dusk: they dart after gnats in the dark.» What is a gnat? | A small bird that sings at dusk | *A tiny flying insect, a bit like a very small fly | A bat's high squeak | A kind of streetlamp
exercise: «Bats catch moths and gnats in the dark.» What do bats do to gnats? | Give them a home | Shout at them to go away | *Catch them | Sing to them
exercise: Where might you see a cloud of gnats? | Deep under the ground | Inside a fridge | *Over water, often on summer evenings | On the top of a mountain
test: In science, how many legs and wings does a gnat have? | *Six legs and two wings | Fins and gills | Fur and four legs | Eight legs and no wings
test: Someone says, «Don't strain at a gnat.» What does this suggest? | Don't be afraid of huge storms | Don't eat any food | *Don't fuss over tiny things | Don't sing loudly in the dark
exam: «Bats catch moths and gnats in the dark.» Which two words in this sentence name small insects? | echoes and squeaks | bats and dark | *moths and gnats | catch and listen
